<ContentLayout
  title="Watch Multiple Kick Streams at Once | Stream Mix"
  description="Watch multiple Kick streams and chats at once. Learn how to add channels, build a flexible layout, and troubleshoot Kick embeds in Stream Mix."
  heading="Watch multiple Kick streams at once"
  platform="kick"
>
  <p>
    Stream Mix displays multiple Kick channels and chats in one customizable
    browser workspace. Arrange creators covering the same game, event, or
    conversation side by side without switching between tabs or manually
    positioning separate browser windows.
  </p>

  <h2>How to add multiple Kick streams</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the creator’s Kick channel page.</li>
    <li>
      Copy its URL, such as <code>https://kick.com/xqc</code>, and paste it into
      the Stream Mix header.
    </li>
    <li>
      Stream Mix selects Kick automatically and extracts the creator’s channel
      name.
    </li>
    <li>Select Stream + Chat, Stream, or Chat and choose Add.</li>
    <li>Repeat for the remaining channels, then arrange their windows.</li>
  </ol>

  <p>
    You can also choose Kick manually and enter only the channel name. Both
    <code>xqc</code> and <code>kick.com/xqc</code> produce the same channel window.
    Stream Mix currently targets live channel pages rather than Kick clips or VODs.
  </p>

  <h2>Choose the right Kick display mode</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Stream + Chat</strong> puts Kick’s player and pop-out chat beside each
      other in one window.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Stream</strong> uses the full panel for video and is useful for secondary
      viewpoints.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Chat</strong> keeps only the conversation visible when you are already
      watching the broadcast elsewhere.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Start with the most important broadcast in a large window, then place
    smaller Stream or Chat panels around it. Windows compact upward after they
    are moved or resized, so you can reorganize the layout without leaving
    unnecessary gaps. Compact mode hides interface chrome, while minimize moves
    a channel to the shelf until you need it again.
  </p>

  <h2>How Kick embeds work</h2>
  <p>
    Video is loaded from Kick’s official
    <code>player.kick.com/CHANNEL</code> embed and chat is loaded from Kick’s pop-out
    chat page. Stream Mix does not copy or restream the broadcast; Kick remains responsible
    for the player, playback controls, chat, account access, and content availability.
  </p>

  <p>
    Kick’s official player supports fullscreen and controls its own autoplay and
    audio behavior. Account or chat features may depend on Kick authentication,
    browser cookie settings, and content-blocking extensions. Kick documents the
    player URL in its
    <a
      href="https://help.kick.com/en/articles/8010826-how-to-embed-your-kick-livestream"
      rel="external">official embedding guide</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>Troubleshoot a Kick stream or chat</h2>
  <h3>The channel is not accepted</h3>
  <p>
    Use the creator’s main channel URL, not a category, search, dashboard, clip,
    or VOD page. You can always select Kick manually and enter the channel name
    that appears directly after <code>kick.com/</code>.
  </p>

  <h3>The player shows an offline channel</h3>
  <p>
    The creator may not be live. You can leave the panel in place because Stream
    Mix saves the channel and its grid position locally for the next session.
  </p>

  <h3>Chat or account controls do not load</h3>
  <p>
    Open the channel directly on Kick to confirm that the service and chat are
    available. If they work there, test Stream Mix without aggressive tracking
    protection or content-blocking extensions. Sending messages may also require
    an authenticated Kick session.
  </p>

  <h3>Several Kick players stutter</h3>
  <p>
    Each live player adds its own video decoding and network load. Mute
    secondary streams, reduce their quality using Kick’s controls, switch some
    windows to Chat only, or minimize panels that you do not need continuously.
  </p>

  <h2>Mix Kick with Twitch and YouTube</h2>
  <p>
    The same layout can contain
    <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-twitch-streams">Twitch channels</a> and
    <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-youtube-streams">YouTube live broadcasts</a
    >. Read the complete <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-streams"
      >multistream viewing guide</a
    >
    for sharing and workspace tips, or visit the <a href="/faq">FAQ</a> for answers
    about saved layouts, privacy, and embeds.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Open the Kick multistream viewer</a>
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
